@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<!-- Global Styles -->
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="~/css/legal/mas-legal.css"
      asp-append-version="true" />
<div class="mas-legal-page">
    <div class="mas-legal-header">
        <span class="mas-legal-eyebrow">LEGAL INFORMATION</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>
            Your privacy matters to us. Learn how MAS Cleaners
            collects, uses and protects your personal information.
        </p>
        <span class="mas-legal-updated">
            Last updated: 12 November 2026
        </span>
    </div>

    <div class="mas-legal-content">

        <section>
            <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                MAS Cleaners ("we", "our" or "us") respects your
                privacy and is committed to protecting your personal
                information.
            </p>
            <p>
                This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use,
                store and protect personal information when you
                visit our website, register an account, request a
                quotation or make a cleaning booking.
            </p>
            <p>
                We process personal information in accordance with
                the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013
                (POPIA) and other applicable South African laws.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>2. Personal Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>
                Depending on the services you request and the type
                of account you hold, we may collect the following:
            </p>

            <h3>2.1 Individual and Contact Information</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>First name and surname.</li>
                <li>Email address.</li>
                <li>Telephone or mobile number.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>2.2 Service and Address Information</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Residential or business service address.</li>
                <li>
                    Additional address information needed to locate
                    the premises where cleaning services will be performed.
                </li>
                <li>Booking details and service-related instructions.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>2.3 Company and Invoicing Information</h3>
            <p>
                For customers booking on behalf of a company or
                business, we may collect:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Company or business name.</li>
                <li>VAT registration number, where applicable.</li>
                <li>Business invoicing information.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>3. Why We Collect Your Information</h2>
            <p>
                We collect and process your information for
                legitimate business and service-related purposes,
                including:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Creating and managing customer accounts.</li>
                <li>Processing and managing cleaning bookings.</li>
                <li>Identifying the premises where services must be performed.</li>
                <li>Communicating booking confirmations, updates and service information.</li>
                <li>Preparing quotations, invoices and payment records.</li>
                <li>Processing and verifying payments.</li>
                <li>Managing cancellations, refunds and customer enquiries.</li>
                <li>Meeting applicable legal, accounting and regulatory obligations.</li>
                <li>Improving our services and customer experience.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>4. How We Process and Share Information</h2>
            <p>
                We do not sell your personal information.
                We only share information where reasonably necessary
                to operate our business, provide the requested
                services or comply with applicable law.
            </p>
            <p>This may include sharing relevant information with:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Authorised MAS Cleaners employees or service
                    personnel who need the information to fulfil
                    your booking.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Payment service providers, including Paystack,
                    when processing online payments.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Financial institutions where necessary to
                    process or verify EFT payments and refunds.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Professional advisers, auditors or authorities
                    where legally required.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Third-party service providers may process information
                in accordance with their own applicable privacy
                policies and contractual obligations.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>5. Online Payments</h2>
            <p>
                Online payments are handled through Paystack.
                Payment processing may require information to be
                shared with Paystack and relevant financial
                institutions.
            </p>
            <p>
                MAS Cleaners uses payment transaction information
                where necessary to confirm payments, reconcile
                bookings and manage refunds.
            </p>
            <p>
                Customers should consult Paystack's privacy and
                security information for details about its own
                processing of payment information.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>6. Protecting Your Personal Information</h2>
            <p>
                We take reasonable and appropriate measures to
                protect personal information against loss,
                unauthorised access, disclosure, alteration or
                destruction.
            </p>
            <p>
                Access to customer information should be limited
                to authorised persons who require it for legitimate
                business purposes.
            </p>
            <p>
                Although we take reasonable steps to protect
                information, no method of electronic storage or
                transmission can be guaranteed to be completely
                secure.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>7. How Long We Keep Your Information</h2>
            <p>
                We retain personal information only for as long
                as reasonably necessary for the purposes for which
                it was collected, including providing services,
                maintaining booking and payment records, resolving
                disputes and meeting legal or accounting obligations.
            </p>
            <p>
                When information is no longer required and there
                is no lawful reason to retain it, we will take
                appropriate steps to delete, destroy or de-identify
                it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>8. Your Rights Under POPIA</h2>
            <p>
                Subject to applicable law, you have the right to:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Know whether we hold your personal information.</li>
                <li>Request access to your personal information.</li>
                <li>Request correction or updating of inaccurate information.</li>
                <li>Request deletion of information where legally permitted.</li>
                <li>Object to certain forms of processing where POPIA allows.</li>
                <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
                <li>Lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Requests relating to your personal information can
                be sent to us using the contact details below.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>9. Cookies and Website Usage</h2>
            <p>
                Our website may use essential cookies or similar
                technologies to support website functionality,
                account authentication and security.
            </p>
            <p>
                Where non-essential cookies or analytics are
                introduced, appropriate information and choices
                will be provided where required by applicable law.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to
                time to reflect changes in our business,
                technology or legal obligations.
            </p>
            <p>
                The latest version will be published on this page.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
            <p>
                If you have questions, concerns or requests
                relating to this Privacy Policy or your personal
                information, contact MAS Cleaners:
            </p>

            <div class="mas-legal-contact">
                <p>
                    <strong>Email:</strong>
                    <a href="mailto:info@mascleaners.co.za">
                        info@mascleaners.co.za
                    </a>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Telephone:</strong>
                    <a href="tel:+27614908391">
                        +27 61 490 8391
                    </a>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Operating area:</strong>
                    Free State, South Africa
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

    </div>
</div>
